  "limitations": [
    "31 input-backlog recoveries are actual corrections, not zero resyncs. They can cause visible local position correction when predicted inputs are discarded.",
    "The SDK driver keeps sending 60Hz commands and consumes authorities; it does not execute browser Game.reconcile or its sequence reset. This cohort demonstrates server queue recovery, not direct forced browser prediction reset coverage.",
    "No persistent 14-command lag appears in the exported monitor; it reaches max10 overall and max9 after recovery, with p95 5. This is an observed finite run, not a guarantee that future input latency is bounded or constant.",
    "All-client ACK aggregates cannot be independently recomputed from the single exported monitor. Before/after monitor windows use an approximate epoch mapping and 1s guard; no motion/ACK array index alignment is assumed.",
    "FPS ranges overlap baseline and moving avatars change LOD/triangles. These sequential samples do not establish causal FPS improvement, discrete GPU performance or 60 FPS.",
    "This is Windows loopback with server, SDK clients and full browser game on one host; public Internet latency/loss and higher capacity remain untested."
  ],
